00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:49.060
However, it's hard for us to build shops
away from watering places.

00:18:49.060 --> 00:18:53.020
So we want a well on Chuo-dori Street,
which is furr from the river.

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:55.560
I didn't look at it that way.

00:18:55.560 --> 00:19:00.650
We wouldn't notice things like this
unless we ask people's opinions, huh?

00:19:00.650 --> 00:19:02.020
Shall we dig a well, then?

00:19:02.020 --> 00:19:05.850
No. If we wanna do something about it,
we should make waterworks.

00:19:05.850 --> 00:19:09.150
How about building an aqueduct running
from the station's platform?

00:19:09.150 --> 00:19:10.270
Good idea!

00:19:10.270 --> 00:19:11.850
Excuse me.

00:19:11.850 --> 00:19:17.440
Will the New Round Table Conference
really be formed in the first place?

00:19:17.440 --> 00:19:17.920
What?

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:22.480
Well, in the poll, the Round Table
supporters were outnumbered, so...

00:19:22.480 --> 00:19:28.230
Hmm... To tell you the truth, I'm leaving
all the election related things to Shiroe.

00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:31.150
My job is figuring things out after winning.

00:19:31.150 --> 00:19:36.020
I feel like I haven't seen
Shiroe much lately, though.

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:40.400
He's most dependable when he's not around.

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:44.150
Yeah! It'll be fine, Isuzu!

00:19:44.150 --> 00:19:45.690
Ahh... Yeah.

00:19:47.350 --> 00:19:50.150
Kinjo, I'd like to discuss something with you.

00:19:50.150 --> 00:19:54.600
About Akiba's city defense system
that's currently being suspended...

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:58.800
Election

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:58.800
Tomorrow!!

00:20:00.940 --> 00:20:03.850
The duke's support in town is unrivaled.

00:20:03.850 --> 00:20:06.270
We don't have to wait till
tomorrow to know the results.

00:20:06.270 --> 00:20:08.440
We'll toast to our victory tonight.

00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:12.600
Eins. Answer my question honestly.

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:14.850
What are our odds of winning right now?

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:16.650
It's probably fifty-fifty.

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:19.730
Don't be ridiculous! How weak-kneed you are!

00:20:19.730 --> 00:20:23.850
It means that's how much
we cannot underestimate our opponent.

00:20:23.850 --> 00:20:25.520
Sage Shiroe...

00:20:25.520 --> 00:20:29.650
It really was a heavy blow that
I could not persuade him that night.

00:20:29.650 --> 00:20:34.230
He didn't take drastic
action during the election,

00:20:34.230 --> 00:20:36.440
and that is rather unsettling.

00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:42.350
I can't tell what he'll do next.
He's always been like that.

00:20:42.350 --> 00:20:44.310
Debauchery Tea Party...

00:20:44.310 --> 00:20:48.520
They conquered numerous raids
before leading guilds did,

00:20:48.520 --> 00:20:52.980
and they did it as if they
decided to do it on a whim.

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:56.190
He was their strategist.

00:20:56.190 --> 00:21:00.520
I admired him, but at the same time,
I was jealous, too.

00:21:00.520 --> 00:21:04.940
As a guild member, I'm not doing
a good job leading the organization.

00:21:04.940 --> 00:21:06.980
I feel useless...

00:21:06.980 --> 00:21:11.190
I appointed you as the Duke of Akiba
because I have confidence in you.

00:21:11.190 --> 00:21:14.400
I did not choose just anyone.

00:21:14.400 --> 00:21:18.100
You even show considerable
concern for peripheral members.

00:21:18.100 --> 00:21:20.350
That is your virtue.

00:21:20.350 --> 00:21:22.060
Sir Touri...

00:21:22.060 --> 00:21:27.850
The Senate kept me useless
in Ikoma for a long time.

00:21:27.850 --> 00:21:30.730
The Saiguu Family does not own
land or soldiers we can freely mobilize.

00:21:30.730 --> 00:21:34.650
We do not have the money
to finance them, either.

00:21:34.650 --> 00:21:39.940
In order to fight the Senate,
I have no choice but to gain Akiba's support.

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:44.730
I'm not intending to fight to lose, of course.

00:21:44.730 --> 00:21:47.150
I'll stand on my battlefield,

00:21:47.150 --> 00:21:51.060
and I'll show you our victory for sure.

00:21:56.940 --> 00:21:58.230
Rayneshia.

00:21:59.480 --> 00:22:00.980
Akatsuki!

00:22:02.100 --> 00:22:03.400
Are you worried?

00:22:03.400 --> 00:22:06.980
I have come this far, so I just have to do it.

00:22:06.980 --> 00:22:09.020
I am nervous, though.

00:22:09.020 --> 00:22:15.060
My lord said this fight was a quest from you.

00:22:15.060 --> 00:22:18.810
He accepted it as a quest,
so he'll carry it out without fail.

00:22:18.810 --> 00:22:22.560
That's how he is. So trust him, Princess.

00:22:27.310 --> 00:22:30.650
At last, tomorrow is the day.

00:22:30.650 --> 00:22:32.060
Right.

00:24:12.730 --> 00:24:15.060
Eins speaks of hope.

00:24:15.060 --> 00:24:18.400
He says the People of the Land and
the Adventurers can help each other.

00:24:18.400 --> 00:24:20.940
Rayneshia speaks of blessing.

00:24:20.940 --> 00:24:24.230
She says Akiba no longer
belongs only to Adventurers

00:24:24.230 --> 00:24:27.400
and the People of the Land
can also support others.

00:24:27.400 --> 00:24:29.770
Together with prayers and wishes...

00:24:29.770 --> 00:24:32.190
Next Time: "Blessings."

00:24:29.860 --> 00:24:36.990
Next Time

00:24:29.860 --> 00:24:36.990
Blessings

00:24:32.190 --> 00:24:35.230
When things go past the
breaking point, rules change.
